WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.968
-House Republicans
are possibly on the verge

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:05.801
of making Ohio Congressman
Jim Jordan,

00:00:05.801 --> 00:00:08.501
one of the key players
in the January 6th coup attempt

00:00:08.501 --> 00:00:11.400
and a hard line MAGA extremist,
the next Speaker of the House,

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.534
even as Trump himself
was just hit

00:00:13.534 --> 00:00:15.434
with his second gag
order by a judge.

00:00:15.434 --> 00:00:17.734
For more on this,
it's time for A Closer Look.

00:00:17.734 --> 00:00:21.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.033 --> 00:00:22.968
House Republicans still don't
have a Speaker

00:00:22.968 --> 00:00:25.601
after two weeks of humiliating
infighting chaos.

00:00:25.601 --> 00:00:27.767
Let's check in
on their party's leader,

00:00:27.767 --> 00:00:30.534
the faraway frontrunner
for the 2024 GOP nomination,

00:00:30.534 --> 00:00:32.033
Donald Trump.

00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:34.467
I mean, there's no way things
could be going worse for him

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:36.634
than they are
for House Republicans, right?

00:00:36.634 --> 00:00:37.968
-Breaking news here
in Washington --

00:00:37.968 --> 00:00:40.601
District Court Judge
Tanya Chutkan

00:00:40.601 --> 00:00:44.467
has issued a narrow gag order
on former President Trump

00:00:44.467 --> 00:00:47.501
and the other co-defendants
in his D.C. election case,

00:00:47.501 --> 00:00:49.234
prohibiting all parties

00:00:49.234 --> 00:00:51.868
from targeting
Special Counsel Jack Smith,

00:00:51.868 --> 00:00:54.167
federal prosecutors,
or court staff.

00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:57.100
-Judge Tanya Chutkan said
from the bench that Mr. Trump

00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:00.834
is now prohibited
from reposting any statements

00:01:00.834 --> 00:01:02.968
publicly targeting
the special counsel,

00:01:02.968 --> 00:01:06.267
his staff, the judge's staff
or court personnel,

00:01:06.267 --> 00:01:08.667
and also witnesses
to the extent

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:11.133
that it involves their role
in the case.

00:01:11.133 --> 00:01:12.300
-That's right.
Trump is prohibited

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.367
from posting statements

00:01:13.367 --> 00:01:15.000
about the special counsel,
his staff,

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.501
the judge's staff, witnesses --

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:17.701
and here's where it gets
worse for him...

00:01:33.367 --> 00:01:37.601
By the way, this is now
Trump's second gag order,

00:01:37.601 --> 00:01:38.834
after he was already
slapped with one

00:01:38.834 --> 00:01:40.400
for a civil fraud trial
in Manhattan.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.767
If he keeps getting hit
with partial gag orders

00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:44.934
from all of his court cases,
his social media posts

00:01:44.934 --> 00:01:46.200
are just going
to look like this.

00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:51.167
Now I don't need to tell you,
we live in turbulent times,

00:01:51.167 --> 00:01:52.868
and times like these,
you need leadership.

00:01:52.868 --> 00:01:54.667
Democrats have Joe Biden
in the White House,

00:01:54.667 --> 00:01:57.133
Chuck Schumer in the Senate, and
Hakeem Jeffries in the House.

00:01:57.133 --> 00:01:58.167
Say what you will about them,

00:01:58.167 --> 00:01:59.868
and there is plenty
to criticize,

00:01:59.868 --> 00:02:02.267
but at least their status
as leaders is stable.

00:02:02.267 --> 00:02:04.000
Now let's compare that
to the GOP leadership.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.801
Likely 2024 nominee
Donald Trump,

00:02:05.801 --> 00:02:08.601
whose current top four suggested
Uber destinations

00:02:08.601 --> 00:02:10.534
are courthouses.

00:02:10.534 --> 00:02:12.467
Senate Minority Leader
Mitch McConnell,

00:02:12.467 --> 00:02:14.267
who can often
be found buffering.

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:17.200
And the Speaker of the House,

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:20.534
which is currently held by
Interim Speaker Patrick McHenry,

00:02:20.534 --> 00:02:22.534
who, knowing the job
isn't permanent,

00:02:22.534 --> 00:02:25.033
is banging every gavel
like it's his last.

00:02:25.033 --> 00:02:26.534
[ Bang ]

00:02:28.367 --> 00:02:31.234
Impossible to prepare
yourself for it.

00:02:31.234 --> 00:02:33.501
The Republican Speaker fight
has been a roller coaster,

00:02:33.501 --> 00:02:35.767
and not a good one.
I'm not talking Kingda Ka,

00:02:35.767 --> 00:02:37.267
where you're laughing
with your buddies, screaming,

00:02:37.267 --> 00:02:38.634
"Oh, my God,
I'm going to puke."

00:02:38.634 --> 00:02:42.334
I'm talking about
one of those real old ones,

00:02:42.334 --> 00:02:43.767
the kinds they have
at county fairs

00:02:43.767 --> 00:02:45.067
where the seat belt
looks like it came

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:48.167
from an '84 Ford Escort,
and you get strapped in

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:49.968
by a dead-eyed
17-year-old

00:02:49.968 --> 00:02:52.701
who reminds you both to keep
your hands inside the vehicle

00:02:52.701 --> 00:02:56.100
and to make peace
with whatever God you pray to.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:58.501
And as you make the first climb,
you look into the footwell

00:02:58.501 --> 00:03:02.567
and you see three loose screws
and a human ankle bone.

00:03:02.567 --> 00:03:05.167
Where you think, "Oh, my God,
I'm going to die.

00:03:05.167 --> 00:03:09.334
I'm going to die listening
to a Jason Aldean cover band."

00:03:09.334 --> 00:03:11.467
And if you do survive afterward,
you check out the photo

00:03:11.467 --> 00:03:15.133
they took and you end up
looking like this.

00:03:15.133 --> 00:03:17.067
Good news, you guys.
Good news.

00:03:17.067 --> 00:03:18.801
If we use that picture
two more times,

00:03:18.801 --> 00:03:20.501
I get a free footlong at Subway.

00:03:20.501 --> 00:03:23.267
Bad news,
it's their new Rudy Sandwich,

00:03:23.267 --> 00:03:24.901
which is just two pieces
of bread

00:03:24.901 --> 00:03:28.934
and a bunch of [bleep] nuts.

00:03:28.934 --> 00:03:32.400
Now here --
here is a quick recap

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:34.033
of what's happened
over the last two years --

00:03:34.033 --> 00:03:35.834
I'm sorry,
I meant the last two weeks.

00:03:35.834 --> 00:03:39.601
-Kevin McCarthy practically
daring hardline Republicans

00:03:39.601 --> 00:03:41.000
to come after him.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.801
-If somebody wants to make
a motion against me, bring it.

00:03:43.801 --> 00:03:46.801
-To which Gaetz responded,
"Just did."

00:03:46.801 --> 00:03:48.868
-He says he's coming for you.
Can you survive?

00:03:48.868 --> 00:03:50.367
-Yes. I'll survive.

00:03:50.367 --> 00:03:53.300
-The Speaker of the House has
been removed from his position.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:56.667
-Some House Republicans
have been in contact with

00:03:56.667 --> 00:03:58.167
and have started an effort

00:03:58.167 --> 00:04:00.734
to draft former
President Donald Trump

00:04:00.734 --> 00:04:01.901
to be the next Speaker.

00:04:04.434 --> 00:04:06.033
-On Capitol Hill right now,
we have breaking news.

00:04:06.033 --> 00:04:07.767
House Republicans have nominated

00:04:07.767 --> 00:04:10.868
Steve Scalise moments ago
as their new Speaker.

00:04:10.868 --> 00:04:13.734
-I want to thank my House
Republican colleagues

00:04:13.734 --> 00:04:17.067
for just designating me
as the Speaker.

00:04:17.067 --> 00:04:19.334
-Just hours after being
nominated to become

00:04:19.334 --> 00:04:22.167
the next Speaker of the House,
Congressman Steve Scalise

00:04:22.167 --> 00:04:24.534
says he's dropping out
of the race.

00:04:24.534 --> 00:04:25.901
-I'm withdrawing my name

00:04:25.901 --> 00:04:28.667
as a candidate
for the Speaker designee.

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:30.634
-Another round of votes
have just been had,

00:04:30.634 --> 00:04:36.000
And now Jim Jordan is the new
Republican nominee for Speaker.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.634
-Right now, it looks like
the party's newest nominee,

00:04:38.634 --> 00:04:40.901
Representative Jim Jordan,

00:04:40.901 --> 00:04:42.534
get this, does not have
enough votes

00:04:42.534 --> 00:04:45.267
from his own GOP colleagues
to win the speakership.

00:04:45.267 --> 00:04:47.267
-I would call House Republicans
a cluster [bleep],

00:04:47.267 --> 00:04:49.634
but a cluster implies
some sense of unity.

00:04:49.634 --> 00:04:52.234
They're more -- they're more
like a scatter [bleep].

00:04:52.234 --> 00:04:55.801
I've seen more organized
groups of seagulls

00:04:55.801 --> 00:04:57.300
fighting over a potato chip.

00:04:57.300 --> 00:04:59.801
"Whoa, whoa, fellas.
Let's just cast our ballots

00:04:59.801 --> 00:05:01.067
in an orderly fashion,

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:03.000
and whoever wins
the most votes gets -- Dorito."

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.801
[ Screaming ]

00:05:04.801 --> 00:05:06.234
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.968 --> 00:05:10.334
You got to --

00:05:10.334 --> 00:05:12.400
you got to remind me
to listen to that seagull tape

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:14.834
before we do the show.

00:05:14.834 --> 00:05:16.067
[ Imitating seagull ] What?

00:05:20.801 --> 00:05:22.801
"Don't worry, Sal,
I can do seagull. Oh-oh."

00:05:26.567 --> 00:05:29.434
I swear to God, if they didn't
have the House to work in,

00:05:29.434 --> 00:05:32.267
I'm not sure half these guys
could find a house to live in.

00:05:32.267 --> 00:05:34.667
You'd just see a pack
of feral Republicans

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:37.167
wandering through the woods,
arguing about which hole

00:05:37.167 --> 00:05:38.701
to [bleep] in.
"Hey, that's my hole.

00:05:38.701 --> 00:05:40.300
I found it first!"

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:41.701
-Usually, a political party

00:05:41.701 --> 00:05:43.133
trying to gain power
in a democracy

00:05:43.133 --> 00:05:45.234
wants to project competence,
even if they have to lie.

00:05:45.234 --> 00:05:47.367
But Republicans are so mad
at each other,

00:05:47.367 --> 00:05:49.200
they're just going on TV
every damn day

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:51.400
telling American people,
"We suck."

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:54.400
-Funding the government is
part of our fundamental duty,

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:55.968
and we can't even do that.

00:05:55.968 --> 00:06:00.133
So, and now here we are at the
11th hour, with a clock ticking,

00:06:00.133 --> 00:06:03.100
and we can't even
seat a speaker.

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:04.567
Man, that says volumes.

00:06:04.567 --> 00:06:06.834
At first, it was
somewhat comical.

00:06:06.834 --> 00:06:11.067
Now it's on -- it's bordering
on the on the absurd.

00:06:11.067 --> 00:06:14.567
-This is not responsible.
We need to elect a Speaker.

00:06:14.567 --> 00:06:16.334
-This is petty. This is petty.

00:06:16.334 --> 00:06:17.801
And I'm getting
freaking tired of this.

00:06:17.801 --> 00:06:20.133
-People are looking
for a perfect system?

00:06:20.133 --> 00:06:21.901
Well, they shouldn't be looking
at the US House right now.

00:06:21.901 --> 00:06:23.334
-How does that
make you guys look?

00:06:23.334 --> 00:06:25.534
-It makes us look like
a bunch of idiots.

00:06:25.534 --> 00:06:27.300
-No, don't worry.
You did already look like

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:29.200
a bunch of idiots,
literally.

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:31.634
South Carolina Congresswoman
Nancy Mace wore the "A"

00:06:31.634 --> 00:06:33.100
on her shirt
for "The Scarlet Letter,"

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:34.701
apparently not having
read the book.

00:06:34.701 --> 00:06:36.968
Wyoming Congresswoman
Harriet Hageman

00:06:36.968 --> 00:06:38.634
brought a lasso
to a GOP meeting,

00:06:38.634 --> 00:06:40.567
hoping to finally catch
one of them Duke boys,

00:06:40.567 --> 00:06:43.167
and Jorge Santos
wore a suit jacket

00:06:43.167 --> 00:06:44.868
over a fleece
over a shirt and tie,

00:06:44.868 --> 00:06:49.234
a fashion crime more heinous
than any of his actual crimes.

00:06:49.234 --> 00:06:51.000
Politicians spend
millions every year

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:53.367
taking out ads to convince
people they should be in charge,

00:06:53.367 --> 00:06:55.701
while Republicans are going on
national TV every day for free,

00:06:55.701 --> 00:06:57.367
telling people
"For the love of God,

00:06:57.367 --> 00:06:59.400
do not put us in charge."

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:00.767
Do you know how rare that is?

00:07:00.767 --> 00:07:02.234
That's like our cue card guy,
Wally,

00:07:02.234 --> 00:07:04.901
saying he doesn't want
a line in the show today.

00:07:04.901 --> 00:07:06.501
Are you sure, Wally?

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:12.400
Because you do still get paid
extra if you say a line.

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:15.868
-Eh.

00:07:15.868 --> 00:07:19.634
-Okay, but for real though,
bits aside,

00:07:19.634 --> 00:07:21.367
how would you solve
this mess in Congress?

00:07:21.367 --> 00:07:23.133
-Well --
-[ Shouts ] Doesn't count.

00:07:23.133 --> 00:07:24.801
[ Laughter ]

00:07:28.567 --> 00:07:29.968
The infighting has
gotten so bad,

00:07:29.968 --> 00:07:31.901
one Republican member
of Congress just came out

00:07:31.901 --> 00:07:34.234
and said what many
have long suspected

00:07:34.234 --> 00:07:35.901
about a large portion
of the Republican Party --

00:07:35.901 --> 00:07:38.334
they don't actually
want to govern.

00:07:38.334 --> 00:07:40.400
-It's a tough scenario,
but there are people in there

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:42.300
that are honorably trying
to get to the right place,

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:44.400
and then there are people
in there, as you know,

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:47.100
that like to go on the TV
and are not necessarily

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:49.300
negotiating for anything
other than TV time.

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:51.100
-These guys want to be
in the minority.

00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:53.501
That's exactly --
I think they would prefer that

00:07:53.501 --> 00:07:54.567
because they can just vote no

00:07:54.567 --> 00:07:56.133
and yell and scream
all the time.

00:07:56.133 --> 00:07:58.901
-Yes. That's the whole party
in a nutshell right there.

00:07:58.901 --> 00:08:01.968
They were Little League
parents screaming at the umpire

00:08:01.968 --> 00:08:03.267
through the chain link fence,

00:08:03.267 --> 00:08:06.634
drunk on Thermos wine
at 8:30 a.m. on a Saturday.

00:08:06.634 --> 00:08:08.267
But now they're the umpire,

00:08:08.267 --> 00:08:09.667
and it's a lot harder
to be the umpire.

00:08:09.667 --> 00:08:10.968
You have to crouch
for three hours,

00:08:10.968 --> 00:08:12.567
keep track of balls
and strikes.

00:08:12.567 --> 00:08:14.901
Then every now and then,
this happens.

00:08:14.901 --> 00:08:16.100
-Hits the 0-1.

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:18.734
Oh!
-Oh, no! Got the umpire.

00:08:18.734 --> 00:08:19.901
-Don't worry.
The umpire didn't die.

00:08:19.901 --> 00:08:22.534
He just wanted to.

00:08:22.534 --> 00:08:25.467
Can we see what his face
looked like under the mask?

00:08:25.467 --> 00:08:27.434
[ Laughter ]

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:34.734
Republicans like yelling
and screaming

00:08:34.734 --> 00:08:36.200
so much more
than governing,

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:38.267
they looked across the country
at all 300 million Americans,

00:08:38.267 --> 00:08:39.767
picked the loudest screamer
and said, "Yeah,

00:08:39.767 --> 00:08:41.367
let's make that guy
the leader of our party."

00:08:41.367 --> 00:08:44.100
A guy who screams so much,
he's now under two gag orders

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:45.601
and still won't shut
the hell up.

00:08:45.601 --> 00:08:47.934
The guy who does all his press
conferences right next to a 747

00:08:47.934 --> 00:08:50.667
just to prove he can
out-yell a jet engine.

00:08:50.667 --> 00:08:53.067
But that really is
the truth right there.

00:08:53.067 --> 00:08:54.734
Republicans are not
a serious governing party

00:08:54.734 --> 00:08:56.367
because they don't have
a serious governing agenda.

00:08:56.367 --> 00:08:58.133
They don't even
have serious options.

00:08:58.133 --> 00:08:59.767
With each failed attempt
to pick a Speaker,

00:08:59.767 --> 00:09:01.734
Republicans don't get together
and say, "We need to do better."

00:09:01.734 --> 00:09:03.300
They say,
"We need to do worse."

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:05.801
And nothing exemplifies
that more than the fact

00:09:05.801 --> 00:09:07.634
Republicans have moved
on to Ohio Congressman

00:09:07.634 --> 00:09:09.400
Jim Jordan,
a MAGA extremist

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:11.300
who tried to overturn
the 2020 election

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:14.367
and played a key role
in the January 6th coup attempt.

00:09:14.367 --> 00:09:17.167
-Jim Jordan scored former
President Trump's endorsement

00:09:17.167 --> 00:09:18.334
early this morning,

00:09:18.334 --> 00:09:20.067
which should come
as no surprise.

00:09:20.067 --> 00:09:22.501
Here is Jordan in Harrisburg,
Pennsylvania,

00:09:22.501 --> 00:09:28.868
attending a Stop the Steal rally
two days after Election Day.

00:09:28.868 --> 00:09:30.734
In the weeks and months
after that,

00:09:30.734 --> 00:09:33.801
Jordan went on various
right wing media outlets,

00:09:33.801 --> 00:09:38.501
where he attempted to sow
distrust in the 2020 election

00:09:38.501 --> 00:09:42.067
and made baseless claims
of election fraud.

00:09:42.067 --> 00:09:45.434
Jordan's name appears
throughout the bipartisan report

00:09:45.434 --> 00:09:47.834
from the House Select committee
investigating January 6th.

00:09:47.834 --> 00:09:49.334
The report says
that Jordan attended

00:09:49.334 --> 00:09:51.434
numerous post-election meetings

00:09:51.434 --> 00:09:54.000
with senior White House
officials and Rudy Giuliani,

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:56.567
discussing how to challenge
the election results.

00:09:56.567 --> 00:09:58.133
-Even if you put aside
the attempted coup

00:09:58.133 --> 00:10:00.334
and Stop the Steal rally,
I think anyone who spends

00:10:00.334 --> 00:10:02.167
any time in a meeting
with Rudy Giuliani

00:10:02.167 --> 00:10:03.634
should be
automatically disqualified.

00:10:03.634 --> 00:10:05.634
Unless that meeting
is an AA meeting,

00:10:05.634 --> 00:10:07.767
although if you told Rudy
to go to AA,

00:10:07.767 --> 00:10:10.000
I guarantee you he'd show up
at an American Airlines flight

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:12.267
with AA batteries.

00:10:12.267 --> 00:10:13.968
And that was today's joke
about Rudy

00:10:13.968 --> 00:10:15.167
mixing up places and things.

00:10:15.167 --> 00:10:16.534
♪♪

00:10:16.534 --> 00:10:18.133
-America!

00:10:20.367 --> 00:10:23.033
Even as Mike Pence, who,
as you may recall,

00:10:23.033 --> 00:10:25.000
and -- [ Laughs ]

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:27.567
[ Laughter ]

00:10:32.901 --> 00:10:35.200
[ Imitates seagull ]

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:36.167
Better?

00:10:38.601 --> 00:10:41.901
Even Mike Pence, who, as you may
recall, and as he maybe doesn't,

00:10:41.901 --> 00:10:43.801
almost got killed by the mob
on January 6th,

00:10:43.801 --> 00:10:45.200
had decided to back Jim Jordan,

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:47.801
despite the fact that Jordan was
on the side of the mob

00:10:47.801 --> 00:10:49.834
and tried to sway Pence
to overturn the election.

00:10:49.834 --> 00:10:52.634
A CNN anchor pointed that out
in an interview with Pence,

00:10:52.634 --> 00:10:54.667
and his answer
was predictably spineless.

00:10:54.667 --> 00:10:56.167
-Jim Jordan would be
an outstanding

00:10:56.167 --> 00:10:57.200
Speaker of the House.

00:10:57.200 --> 00:10:58.534
The American people want to see

00:10:58.534 --> 00:11:00.200
the Republican conference
come together,

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:01.868
elect a speaker,
and get back to work.

00:11:01.868 --> 00:11:04.200
-Well, it's interesting to me
to hear you say that

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:06.334
Jim Jordan would be
a great speaker,

00:11:06.334 --> 00:11:07.667
given he was someone

00:11:07.667 --> 00:11:10.968
who sent a text to the chief
of staff on January 5th

00:11:10.968 --> 00:11:14.467
that outlined for you
to violate the Constitution

00:11:14.467 --> 00:11:16.400
and block the certification
of the election.

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:17.767
I mean, do you really believe
that's someone

00:11:17.767 --> 00:11:21.834
who should be third in line
to the presidency?

00:11:21.834 --> 00:11:23.734
-I have immense respect
for Jim Jordan.

00:11:23.734 --> 00:11:27.667
He's a man of integrity, and
I've known him for many years.

00:11:27.667 --> 00:11:29.801
I was not aware
of his opinion

00:11:29.801 --> 00:11:31.767
going into January 6th --
-So that doesn't bother you?

00:11:31.767 --> 00:11:34.434
-My interaction with
Congressman Jordan in December

00:11:34.434 --> 00:11:37.934
was simply over
the legitimate objections

00:11:37.934 --> 00:11:42.367
that members of Congress were
permitted to file under the law.

00:11:42.367 --> 00:11:45.133
-"Of all the people
who fomented a violent mob

00:11:45.133 --> 00:11:46.434
intent on murdering me,

00:11:46.434 --> 00:11:51.367
there is none I consider
a better man than Jim Jordan.

00:11:51.367 --> 00:11:55.133
It would be an honor to be
murdered by him." [ Laughs ]

00:11:55.133 --> 00:11:57.434
Pence's problem is there are
no other options.

00:11:57.434 --> 00:11:58.467
Here's a perfect example.

00:11:58.467 --> 00:12:00.234
Republican Congressman
Dan Crenshaw

00:12:00.234 --> 00:12:02.400
made the case for Jim Jordan
to CNN's Jake Tapper,

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:04.267
who pointed out that,
unlike Crenshaw,

00:12:04.267 --> 00:12:06.200
Jordan pressured Pence
to overturn the election.

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:09.167
And Crenshaw basically said
if that disqualified him,

00:12:09.167 --> 00:12:10.534
there wouldn't be anyone else.

00:12:10.534 --> 00:12:13.000
-I'm supporting Jordan.
I'm going to vote for Jordan.

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:15.567
-I mean, he defied
the congressional subpoena,

00:12:15.567 --> 00:12:18.234
and he was trying to get Pence
to overturn the electoral votes.

00:12:18.234 --> 00:12:20.434
But anyway, you're -- you're --
in the --

00:12:20.434 --> 00:12:22.667
you're in the Jordan camp.
-But a lot of them did that.

00:12:22.667 --> 00:12:24.067
If I held that grudge,

00:12:24.067 --> 00:12:25.834
I wouldn't have friends
in the Republican conference.

00:12:25.834 --> 00:12:27.400
-Right, that two-thirds of --
-That's a lot of them.

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:28.400
-That's two thirds
of the conference.

00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:30.467
That's an excellent point.

00:12:30.467 --> 00:12:32.801
-I was on an island there.
-Yeah, I hear you.

00:12:32.801 --> 00:12:34.601
-I love how they're both
laughing off

00:12:34.601 --> 00:12:36.100
that deeply depressing fact.

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:38.701
But it is a fact.
There are very few Republicans

00:12:38.701 --> 00:12:40.968
who didn't try to overturn
the 2020 election at this point.

00:12:40.968 --> 00:12:42.467
Being a Republican
who thinks Biden won

00:12:42.467 --> 00:12:43.868
is like being
a vegan zombie --

00:12:43.868 --> 00:12:47.968
"Do you have anything
other than brains?"

00:12:47.968 --> 00:12:49.734
That is the core
of the modern GOP.

00:12:49.734 --> 00:12:51.367
It's not a serious
or competent party

00:12:51.367 --> 00:12:53.267
that can be trusted with
the responsibility to govern.

00:12:53.267 --> 00:12:56.000
As far as anyone can tell,
their only discernible position

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:59.334
is that January 6th was good,
and anyone involved in that,

00:12:59.334 --> 00:13:01.200
whether it's Jim Jordan
or Donald Trump,

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:02.734
should be in a position
of leadership.

00:13:02.734 --> 00:13:04.334
Their pitch to the American
people is,

00:13:04.334 --> 00:13:05.868
"Elect us because we're a..."

00:13:05.868 --> 00:13:07.000
-Bunch of idiots.

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:09.434
-This has been A Closer Look.

00:13:09.434 --> 00:13:12.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

